=== (2) multi-band mixing: reduction lemma and the su(2) ('rotation-like') mixing ===
  spin-1 Pi_j = S_j: |[S_x,S_y] - i S_z| = 0.0e+00; spec S_x = [-1.  0.  1.] (k-independent)
  G m=0.3: spin-1 multiplet, max_k |v_i S_j - v_j S_i| = 0.981 (0 needed for symmetric T^ij -> v = 0: flat band)
  NN m=1.0: spin-1 multiplet, max_k |v_i S_j - v_j S_i| = 0.607 (0 needed for symmetric T^ij -> v = 0: flat band)
  zigzag {+tri,-tri}, shifts {+q,-q}, q=1e-01: partner violation max = 9.99e-02 (= 1.00 q) at k = +3.0916 (peak k = +-pi); violation at |k|<2.5: 5.6e-16
  zigzag {+tri,-tri}, shifts {+q,-q}, q=1e-02: partner violation max = 9.95e-03 (= 0.99 q) at k = +3.1366 (peak k = +-pi); violation at |k|<2.5: 8.9e-16
  zigzag {+tri,-tri}, shifts {+q,-q}, q=1e-03: partner violation max = 7.43e-04 (= 0.74 q) at k = +3.1410 (peak k = +-pi); violation at |k|<2.5: 5.6e-16

=== (3) field-dependent generators: Poisson-bracket check of the 'graviton inverse propagator' structure ===
  pi-coefficient of {Q, Hm+Hg}: (ai*bi + ar*br)*(Y*c + Z*e1 - Z*e2)
  require it = 0  ->  Y = [Z*(-e1 + e2)/c]
  h-coefficient after that: Z*(ai*br - ar*bi)*(Kq*c - e1**2 + 2*e1*e2 - e2**2)/c   (omega = e2 - e1; factor (c*Kq - omega^2)/c * Z = graviton inverse propagator at (omega, q) times Z: zero only for an on-shell graviton)

=== (4) energy-shell (field-dependent) form, single band: t.grad(Pi_x) = t_x for t tangent to the energy surface ===
